Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.95,0:13:52.20,Announcement,,0,0,0,,Ship has moved to Alert Status 1.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.20,0:13:55.21,Announcement,,0,0,0,,Repeat: Ship has moved to Alert Status 1.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.21,0:13:58.42,Announcement,,0,0,0,,The Garmiroid we recovered has escaped the analysis room.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.42,0:14:01.23,Announcement,,0,0,0,,It is hiding somewhere aboard the ship.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.46,0:14:04.23,Announcement,,0,0,0,,Security teams are to capture or destroy it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.46,0:14:08.22,Announcement,,0,0,0,,Repeat: Security teams are to capture or destroy it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.97,0:01:37.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, on {\i1}Yamato Radio Theater,{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.30,0:01:40.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone calling themselves Shiro Shinta has requested
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.64,0:01:42.71,Default,,0,0,0,,one of the famous late 21st century stories,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.94,0:01:45.69,Default,,0,0,0,,"The Heart of Observer #9."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.73,0:01:51.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Back when there were still no towns on Mars,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.69,0:01:56.65,Default,,0,0,0,,a single observation station stood alone, at the edge of Mare Sirenum.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.20,0:02:03.64,Default,,0,0,0,,No one ever visited this forgotten tower,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.64,0:02:10.00,Default,,0,0,0,,where a single, young observer lived like a lighthouse keeper.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.79,0:02:16.51,Default,,0,0,0,,He had no name, only the number "9."
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.51,0:02:19.51,Default,,0,0,0,,A Clockwork Parable
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.68,0:02:28.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Transferring visual sensors from Garmiroid A to Garmiroid B.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.73,0:02:37.53,Default,,0,0,0,,It worked.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.66,0:02:42.45,Default,,0,0,0,,All three Garmiroid soldiers we recovered on Enceladus
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.45,0:02:47.54,Default,,0,0,0,,were automata with orthodox AIs.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.54,0:02:48.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Automata?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.83,0:02:50.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Mechanical dolls, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.83,0:02:53.92,Default,,0,0,0,,By running a massive number of simple programs in parallel,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.92,0:02:58.01,Default,,0,0,0,,it can perform complex actions just like humans do.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.30,0:03:03.68,Default,,0,0,0,,They share the same fundamental architecture as our artificial intelligences.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.01,0:03:06.93,Default,,0,0,0,,So we know Garmillas uses the same mathematics
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.93,0:03:09.23,Default,,0,0,0,,and understanding of physics that we do.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.23,0:03:12.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Their culture should be one we can communicate with.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.27,0:03:18.36,Default,,0,0,0,,When you encounter a foreign civilization in space, this is very important.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.82,0:03:21.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Especially in times of war.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.32,0:03:26.79,Default,,0,0,0,,It lets us play shogi by the same rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.33,0:03:28.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.41,0:03:31.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Did we manage to salvage any other information?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.75,0:03:33.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Such as enemy positions?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.96,0:03:40.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, two of their storage units were too badly damaged for repair.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.09,0:03:45.55,Default,,0,0,0,,The other's survived, but the data is only accessible from a Garmillas mainframe.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.01,0:03:47.64,Default,,0,0,0,,But then...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.06,0:03:49.64,Default,,0,0,0,,However, there is a way.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.31,0:03:54.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Have the Garmiroid tell us.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.90,0:03:56.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Mainframe restored.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.36,0:03:59.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Rebooting Garmiroid Alternative.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.28,0:04:08.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you hear me?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.95,0:04:13.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I am Type AU09, the sub-frame of this ship.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.79,0:04:16.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Please call me Analyzer.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.71,0:04:21.76,Default,,0,0,0,,A... A-An... An-Analyzer?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.34,0:04:28.01,Default,,0,0,0,,You are a rebooted, alternative version of a foreign civilization's servant android.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.01,0:04:31.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I know... I'll call you Alter!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.31,0:04:33.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Alter...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.32,0:04:39.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Warp complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.73,0:04:41.86,Default,,0,0,0,,No enemies in immediate vicinity.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.15,0:04:46.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Sanada, I will return to analyzing Alter.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.37,0:04:47.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Go ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.32,0:04:48.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.62,0:04:51.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Analyzer appears to be enjoying himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.04,0:04:52.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sure he is.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.62,0:04:55.12,Default,,0,0,0,,He has another machine to talk to.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.37,0:04:56.79,Default,,0,0,0,,What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.79,0:04:57.63,Default,,0,0,0,,A cat.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.92,0:05:00.92,Default,,0,0,0,,No, no. This is a dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.92,0:05:02.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Dogs are mammals.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.51,0:05:04.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Mammals are animals.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.68,0:05:07.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Mammal. Animal.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.64,0:05:08.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Then what is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.10,0:05:09.64,Default,,0,0,0,,A dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.89,0:05:12.35,Default,,0,0,0,,No, this is a cat.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.35,0:05:15.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Analyzer. Are you two machines having a secret chat?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.85,0:05:17.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing of the sort.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.65,0:05:20.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I am teaching Alter to speak.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.36,0:05:22.25,Default,,0,0,0,,To speak, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.25,0:05:27.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You were able to link operating systems, so just import the dictionary data.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.11,0:05:29.66,Default,,0,0,0,,The names alone are not enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.66,0:05:35.21,Default,,0,0,0,,To understand a concept, large numbers of exchanges are required.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.21,0:05:36.04,Default,,0,0,0,,And...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.29,0:05:37.62,Default,,0,0,0,,That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.62,0:05:41.02,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't connect it to the ship's network.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.51,0:05:48.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I was right. We didn't investigate enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.89,0:05:51.64,Default,,0,0,0,,This doesn't tell me if we can colonize it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.31,0:05:58.48,Default,,0,0,0,,One day, an old mechanical engineer named Houdin
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.48,0:06:02.02,Default,,0,0,0,,appeared at the observatory with a girl named Eve.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.73,0:06:05.28,Default,,0,0,0,,The meeting was magical.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.99,0:06:08.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Following the sound of a song to the sea,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.20,0:06:12.99,Default,,0,0,0,,#9 saw a girl sitting on a rock, singing.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.02,0:06:36.81,Default,,0,0,0,,"Wh-Who?"
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.52,0:06:41.56,Default,,0,0,0,,She turned and asked,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.90,0:06:44.94,Default,,0,0,0,,"Who are you?"
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.03,0:06:50.03,Default,,0,0,0,,"What are you doing out here?"
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.29,0:07:00.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I met a goddess yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.37,0:07:01.33,Default,,0,0,0,,A goddess?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.42,0:07:04.67,Default,,0,0,0,,The goddess of this ship.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.71,0:07:07.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Who might that be?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.80,0:07:11.01,Default,,0,0,0,,They asked, "Who are you?"
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.01,0:07:14.47,Default,,0,0,0,,And I replied, "I am Alter."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.47,0:07:18.73,Default,,0,0,0,,And they said, "I am not asking for your name."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.27,0:07:21.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Operations Officer Mori, perhaps?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.81,0:07:23.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Or Miss Niimi?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.90,0:07:24.94,Default,,0,0,0,,No, that's impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.02,0:07:28.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you answer it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.86,0:07:30.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.61,0:07:33.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I am...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.66,0:07:37.91,Default,,0,0,0,,This is Shinohara.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.50,0:07:40.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm investigating the spatial wake in front of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.83,0:07:42.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I've confirmed that it's safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.42,0:07:43.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Roger.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.46,0:07:47.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Shinohara and Yamamoto\Ncompleting patrol and returning to ship.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.51,0:07:50.38,Default,,0,0,0,,When both have returned,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.38,0:07:53.05,Default,,0,0,0,,we will move to warp navigation at 0200.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.34,0:07:54.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Roger.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.34,0:07:56.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Prepare for docking.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.56,0:07:58.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Analyzer, give them a hand, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.56,0:08:00.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Roger.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.03,0:08:09.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I win.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.03,0:08:12.78,Default,,0,0,0,,They're back.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.78,0:08:13.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.41,0:08:17.78,Default,,0,0,0,,No fair! I had a straight flush!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.39,0:08:42.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Navi, handle the automatic docking guidance for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.02,0:08:45.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Switching to automatic control.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.31,0:08:46.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks, Navi.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.02,0:08:51.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Just now, you were thinking that I'm nuts, weren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.57,0:08:52.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I was not.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.86,0:08:56.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Name them, take care of them, and they'll do good work for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.74,0:08:58.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Exactly like anyone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.99,0:09:00.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Open hatch, port side.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.70,0:09:02.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, let's get started.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.17,0:09:09.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Guidance team, prepare to pull them in.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.88,0:09:12.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.60,0:09:25.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Alter?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.28,0:09:35.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Toyama, is there an error on the control panel?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.28,0:09:38.28,Default,,0,0,0,,The monitor's down.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.28,0:09:39.41,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.83,0:09:47.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Force purge!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.92,0:09:48.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Purging-
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.79,0:09:52.00,Default,,0,0,0,,What the heck?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.46,0:09:53.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Toyama!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.47,0:09:58.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Shinohara!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.34,0:09:59.30,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm on it!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.19,0:10:10.48,Default,,0,0,0,,What's wrong with you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.48,0:10:11.98,Default,,0,0,0,,What were you thinking?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.98,0:10:14.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Um, well... I really don't know what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.28,0:10:18.03,Default,,0,0,0,,That crane's movements are controlled by a program, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.41,0:10:19.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, they are.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.99,0:10:24.24,Default,,0,0,0,,But for some reason, the system monitor went down today.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.24,0:10:27.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Normally, they should shut down automatically.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.29,0:10:29.04,Default,,0,0,0,,This has never happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.04,0:10:29.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You morons!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.13,0:10:31.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Just because it's never happened before
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.79,0:10:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,doesn't mean it won't happen today!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.00,0:10:36.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Why do you think we have humans there to help the machines?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.80,0:10:37.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.38,0:10:40.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, both of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.76,0:10:42.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Forgive us.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.01,0:10:45.47,Default,,0,0,0,,No... I mean, you're taking it seriously...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.89,0:10:46.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.39,0:10:47.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Y-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.61,0:10:58.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Before the accident, you were talking to Alter via network, weren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.70,0:10:59.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.70,0:11:03.87,Default,,0,0,0,,There was a very minor delay in the\Nprocess that feeds hangar information
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.87,0:11:06.20,Default,,0,0,0,,back to the mainframe.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.20,0:11:08.33,Default,,0,0,0,,That caused the arm malfunction.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.71,0:11:10.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm terribly sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.04,0:11:15.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Your conversations with Alter may be stressing the system unexpectedly.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.05,0:11:18.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Should this keep happening, I'll have to reformat you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.72,0:11:20.38,Default,,0,0,0,,That would be...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.39,0:11:25.35,Default,,0,0,0,,...the correct decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.06,0:11:30.02,Default,,0,0,0,,We're done analyzing Alter for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.40,0:11:36.86,Default,,0,0,0,,You're forbidden from coming here or speaking to Alter via network.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.23,0:11:39.07,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll keep an eye on things for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.70,0:11:40.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Got it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.20,0:11:41.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.33,0:11:56.25,Default,,0,0,0,,The old man sent Eve back, on board the ship.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.25,0:12:00.09,Default,,0,0,0,,And the observer desired nothing more than to see her again.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.01,0:12:05.72,Default,,0,0,0,,For the first time in his life, he understood loneliness.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.76,0:12:10.85,Default,,0,0,0,,He decided to go and see Eve.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.39,0:12:17.71,Default,,0,0,0,,He felt that this was the only way to learn who he was.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.70,0:12:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Sanada, I learned something from talking with Alter.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.79,0:12:39.13,Default,,0,0,0,,They are just like me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.13,0:12:40.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.13,0:12:47.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Alter asked me who I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.47,0:12:48.51,Default,,0,0,0,,What did you tell him?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.51,0:12:50.72,Default,,0,0,0,,A friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.06,0:12:54.14,Default,,0,0,0,,A friend, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.19,0:12:56.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Good answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.54,0:13:13.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is the goddess?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.35,0:13:33.08,Default,,0,0,0,,What has happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.08,0:13:35.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Apparently, the lock to the analysis room has been destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.90,0:13:40.36,Default,,0,0,0,,That Garmiroid...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.90,0:13:42.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Send security at once!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.53,0:13:49.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Weapons approved, where appropriate!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.71,0:14:04.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.71,0:14:05.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.43,0:14:10.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't move. Stay right there.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.64,0:14:17.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Target acquired!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.77,0:14:19.90,Default,,0,0,0,,It's fleeing on the port side deck 3!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.94,0:14:29.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Alter wanted to know who he was.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.28,0:14:33.45,Default,,0,0,0,,He must think if he finds the goddess, he will learn.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.45,0:14:34.58,Default,,0,0,0,,The goddess?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.45,0:14:39.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Alter said she was the goddess of this ship.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.75,0:14:45.59,Default,,0,0,0,,And I learned one other important thing about the Garmiroids...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.59,0:14:50.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't let him escape. Seal the bulkheads.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.02,0:14:57.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't move!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.11,0:15:04.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Mori, where is the Garmiroid soldier?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.28,0:15:08.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Heading straight toward the ship's bow, via the deck 2 ducts.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.41,0:15:12.45,Default,,0,0,0,,We're heading toward the sealed room, aren't we?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.95,0:15:15.99,Default,,0,0,0,,It contains the automatic guidance systems to take us to Iscandar.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.99,0:15:17.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that his objective?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.41,0:15:17.95,Default,,0,0,0,,There he is!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.54,0:15:21.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't let him reach it! Destroy him if you must!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.76,0:15:30.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Enemy...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.09,0:15:32.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Terror...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.39,0:15:33.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Being...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.01,0:15:34.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Goddess!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.31,0:15:46.44,Default,,0,0,0,,The Garmiroid has entered the second turret loading room.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.03,0:15:50.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Well?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.82,0:15:52.86,Default,,0,0,0,,No good. It's locked from the inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.86,0:15:55.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Bridge, get that lock open!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.49,0:15:56.99,Default,,0,0,0,,As soon as it opens, we fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.62,0:15:58.43,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the bridge.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.79,0:16:01.67,Default,,0,0,0,,He's infiltrated our security and locked it from the inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.29,0:16:04.69,Default,,0,0,0,,It will take some time to unlock it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.88,0:16:07.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Please stand by.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.84,0:16:10.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Perfect timing, AU09. Open the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.97,0:16:13.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Before that, put your guns away.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.47,0:16:14.55,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.55,0:16:17.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't want him to think we're enemies.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.18,0:16:20.27,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about? Of course we're enemies.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.27,0:16:22.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Will you kill an unresisting prisoner?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.10,0:16:24.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Misaki?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.02,0:16:25.61,Default,,0,0,0,,A prisoner?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.61,0:16:26.86,Default,,0,0,0,,That's stupid.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.86,0:16:28.63,Default,,0,0,0,,It's just a robot.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.03,0:16:32.13,Default,,0,0,0,,If it has a heart, even a machine should be treated as a prisoner.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.45,0:16:35.07,Default,,0,0,0,,A heart? It has a heart?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.07,0:16:37.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I was told it was an automaton.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.16,0:16:39.89,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what the XO said.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.54,0:16:42.12,Default,,0,0,0,,It's true that the Garmiroids
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.12,0:16:45.88,Default,,0,0,0,,are automata that function by running massive numbers of programs.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.17,0:16:49.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Correct? Machines are just machines.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.17,0:16:53.43,Default,,0,0,0,,But we cannot say for certain that our brains
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.43,0:16:57.28,Default,,0,0,0,,are not also automata that function via parallel processing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.35,0:16:59.93,Default,,0,0,0,,It seems you want to believe that
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.93,0:17:04.69,Default,,0,0,0,,their processing circuitry cannot give rise to a consciousness like ours.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.69,0:17:10.80,Default,,0,0,0,,However, you cannot actually prove that that's the case.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.41,0:17:18.74,Default,,0,0,0,,An interesting story.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.74,0:17:21.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I've retaken control of the security.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.37,0:17:24.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Anyway, for the moment, put away your weapons.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.17,0:17:27.75,Default,,0,0,0,,If you say so, XO.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.75,0:17:29.31,Default,,0,0,0,,The door will open.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.85,0:17:39.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Misaki?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.93,0:17:47.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Sanada, I recommend that Alter be shut down immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.65,0:17:49.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Why is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.11,0:17:54.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Alter may commit suicide.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.61,0:18:01.85,Default,,0,0,0,,He is programmed to self-destruct if isolated and surrounded by enemies.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.20,0:18:04.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop him!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.12,0:18:07.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Analyzer, let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.54,0:18:08.48,Default,,0,0,0,,XO Sanada.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.09,0:18:15.74,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't think it has a heart, do you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.84,0:18:23.24,Default,,0,0,0,,To me, it remains unclear whether even you have a heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.65,0:18:32.75,Default,,0,0,0,,It may be that you don't have a heart like I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.48,0:18:36.99,Default,,0,0,0,,You could just be simulating a human.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.15,0:18:40.16,Default,,0,0,0,,The Garmiroid soldier has exited the ship.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.62,0:18:43.16,Default,,0,0,0,,It's moving along the upper deck, toward the bridge.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.79,0:18:47.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't allow it to get near the automatic guidance system.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.00,0:18:49.35,Default,,0,0,0,,We will destroy it if we must.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.55,0:19:40.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Shell block destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.22,0:19:41.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Infiltrating kernel.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.93,0:19:45.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.56,0:19:46.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Cat.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.22,0:19:48.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Being.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.89,0:19:50.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Goddess.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.48,0:19:51.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Death.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.10,0:19:59.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Fr... ie... n... d...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.87,0:20:07.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Garmiroid Alternative has been shut down.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.91,0:20:11.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Mainframe has been reformatted and cannot be rebooted.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.41,0:20:13.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Recover its task log.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.12,0:20:14.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Roger.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.74,0:20:47.62,Default,,0,0,0,,The analysis is complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.99,0:20:53.92,Default,,0,0,0,,We found nothing in Alter's task log to indicate an activated booby trap.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.92,0:20:55.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Then...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.71,0:20:56.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.09,0:21:04.65,Default,,0,0,0,,If nothing else, he believed he still had at least one friend on this ship.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.40,0:21:19.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Eve's skin was peeled away, her joints torn off,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.32,0:21:24.15,Default,,0,0,0,,revealing a body of gears and silicon.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.74,0:21:33.00,Default,,0,0,0,,From the tower's window, #9 watched her sink into the Mare Sirenum.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.87,0:21:40.44,Default,,0,0,0,,"I no longer feel pity for that doll.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.84,0:21:49.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Because I know that I am also one, created by Houdin,"
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.85,0:21:57.96,Default,,0,0,0,,he thought to himself, alone in his\Nsmall room in the observation station.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.11,0:22:04.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Whether that beautiful doll did or did not have a heart,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.24,0:22:08.87,Default,,0,0,0,,it didn't matter to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.03,0:22:12.99,Default,,0,0,0,,And he thought this, as well...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.45,0:22:15.98,Default,,0,0,0,,"The fact that I have a heart
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.87,0:22:21.00,Default,,0,0,0,,is a secret that belongs only to me."
Dialogue: 0,0:24:11.32,0:24:16.62,Default,,0,0,0,,The Yamato plunges through a\Ndimensional gap, into a ship's graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:16.62,0:24:18.91,Default,,0,0,0,,A cruel space, devoid of life.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.91,0:24:22.08,Default,,0,0,0,,And there, the shadow of an enemy ship appears.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.08,0:24:24.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Will they work together or against one other?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:24.25,0:24:29.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Will men be able to work together, rather than wait for death?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:30.01,0:24:33.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Next time: Graveyard of the Universe.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:33.13,0:24:38.39,Default,,0,0,0,,There are 325 days left before humanity is extinct.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.34,0:22:46.34,ED,,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,500)}That girl was waving
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.34,0:22:50.68,ED,,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,500)}A bright {\c&H0000FF&}red scarf
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.68,0:22:58.86,ED,,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,500)}Who do you think it was for?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.86,0:23:02.86,ED,,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,500)}Whoever it was
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.86,0:23:06.99,ED,,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,500)}It doesn’t matter
Dialogue: 0,0:23:06.99,0:23:15.29,ED,,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,500)}Let each think it was for him
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.29,0:23:23.59,ED,,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,500)}The hearts of men beginning a journey
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.59,0:23:30.60,ED,,0,1100,0,,{\fad(500,500)}Want a piece of romance
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.67,0:23:50.49,ED,,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1000)}A bright {\c&H0000FF&}red scarf
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.48,0:22:29.45,EP TS,,0,0,0,,{\blur7.5\shad0\blur7.5\3aH&90&\4aH&99&\fade(2500,1500)}{\pos(1183,840)}Episode 9
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.48,0:22:29.45,EP TS,,0,0,0,,{\blur7.5\shad0\blur7.5\3aH&90&\4aH&99&\fade(2500,1500)}{\pos(1183,1073)}Clockwork Prisoner
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.24,0:00:21.71,OP,,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,200)\blur7\be2}Farewell, Earth
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.71,0:00:28.97,OP,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\blur7\be2}The ship that is departing is
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.97,0:00:36.64,OP,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\blur7\be2}The Space Battleship
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.64,0:00:42.69,OP,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,2000)\blur7\be2}Yamato
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.32,0:00:47.94,OP,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\blur7\pos(777,60)\be2}It departs now to Iscandar,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.94,0:00:52.66,OP,,900,0,0,,{\an9\fad(200,200)\blur7\be2}at the end of the cosmos,\Nbearing its fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.66,0:00:59.79,OP,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\blur7\be2}"We will come back, no matter what it takes"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.00,0:01:08.72,OP,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\blur7\be2}Answer with a smile to the waving people
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.42,0:01:13.22,OP,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\blur7\be2}Going far from the Galaxy towards Iscandar
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.22,0:01:16.64,OP,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\blur7\be2}A faint gleam of hope
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.64,0:01:24.23,OP,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,3000)\blur7\be2}The Space Battleship Yamato
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.71,0:01:47.59,TS Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,4000)\an8\blur4\shad0\c&H749481&\3c&H1E161D&}"The Heart of Observer #9."
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.06,0:05:56.31,TS Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8\bord2\shad0\c&HA9BEAE&\blur3\3c&H6E7065&}Do Automata Dream of Electric Sheep?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.08,0:12:29.58,TS Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8\bord2\shad0\c&HA9BEAE&\blur3\3c&H6E7065&}I, Robot
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.44,0:15:48.86,TS Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8\bord2\shad0\c&HA9BEAE&\blur3\3c&H6E7065&}Flow My Tears, the Automata Said
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.75,0:21:14.69,TS Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8\bord2\shad0\c&HA9BEAE&\blur3\3c&H6E7065&}{\fad(700,0)}The Heart of Observer #9
